From: Mohit Sharma <mohit.sharma@oss.qualcomm.com>
Subject: [PATCH] soc: qcom: apr: publish the GPR callback before client probe

Both patches of "Fix GPR callback registration race during probe", in upstream
order:

 1/2 ASoC: qcom: q6apm: Guard callbacks until probe data is ready
     <20261022144130.2443667-2-mohit.sharma@oss.qualcomm.com>
 2/2 soc: qcom: apr: Publish GPR callback before client probe
     <20261022144130.2443667-3-mohit.sharma@oss.qualcomm.com>

A GPR service driver can issue synchronous commands from its probe path, but
the bus only installed the service callback after probe returned. A response
arriving in between found a NULL callback and was dropped, and the client timed
out:

  qcom-apm ... CMD timeout for [1001021] opcode

The second patch installs the callback before probe, clears it again if probe
fails, and leaves APR clients as they were. That lets a callback run before the
client has published its data, so the first patch makes q6apm publish its
driver data last, and q6apm and q6prm ignore packets until it is there. q6apm
and q6prm are the only GPR clients. The two only make sense together.

Fixes: ec1471a898cc ("soc: qcom: apr: Add GPR support")
Cc: stable@vger.kernel.org
Co-developed-by: Ajay Kumar Nandam <ajay.nandam@oss.qualcomm.com>
Signed-off-by: Ajay Kumar Nandam <ajay.nandam@oss.qualcomm.com>
Signed-off-by: Mohit Sharma <mohit.sharma@oss.qualcomm.com>
---
diff --git a/drivers/soc/qcom/apr.c b/drivers/soc/qcom/apr.c
index ea7f83916..829e5c8fd 100644
--- a/drivers/soc/qcom/apr.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/qcom/apr.c
@@ -365,13 +365,24 @@ static int apr_device_probe(struct device *dev)
 {
 	struct apr_device *adev = to_apr_device(dev);
 	struct apr_driver *adrv = to_apr_driver(dev->driver);
+	struct packet_router *apr = dev_get_drvdata(dev->parent);
 	int ret;
 
+	if (apr->type == PR_TYPE_GPR)
+		adev->svc.callback = adrv->gpr_callback;
+
 	ret = adrv->probe(adev);
-	if (!ret)
+	if (ret) {
+		if (apr->type == PR_TYPE_GPR)
+			adev->svc.callback = NULL;
+
+		return ret;
+	}
+
+	if (apr->type != PR_TYPE_GPR)
 		adev->svc.callback = adrv->gpr_callback;
 
-	return ret;
+	return 0;
 }
 
 static void apr_device_remove(struct device *dev)
diff --git a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6apm.c b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6apm.c
